workedExamples.question_text:
The graph of $y=g(x)$ is shown. Evaluate (a) $g(1)$ and (b) $g(-1)+g(1)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-3.5,0)--(3.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,5.5);
\path (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}{\draw[black] (\x,-0.08)--(\x,0.08);\path (\x,-0.08) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5}{\draw[black] (-0.08,\y)--(0.08,\y);\path (-0.08,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\path (0,0) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[black,thick,<-] (-3,5)--(1,1);
\draw[black,fill=white] (1,1) circle[radius=2pt];
\draw[black,thick,->] (1,4)--(3,4);
\fill[black] (1,4) circle[radius=2pt];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-1,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-3,1) -- (0,2);
\fill (0,2) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[thick, ->] (0,4) -- (3.5,0.5);
\draw[fill=white] (0,4) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $f(0)$.

The graph of $y = h(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.5) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-3,-1) -- (2,4);
\fill (2,4) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[thick, ->] (2,1) -- (4,-1);
\draw[fill=white] (2,1) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $h(2)$.

